# Cursor Rules for 101 Jiu Jitsu Website

## Project Context
- Martial arts gym website for 101 Jiu Jitsu & Kickboxing in Goleta, CA
- Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, deployed to Vercel
- Mobile-first, responsive design

## Brand Guidelines
- Primary Red: #E42416
- Primary Dark: #C41E1A
- Secondary (Dark): #0a1628
- Accent Blue: #1e3a8a
- White: #ffffff
- Font: Oswald (headings, uppercase), Inter (body)

## Architecture
- Global nav: components/Header.tsx — NEVER duplicate nav HTML in pages
- Global footer: components/Footer.tsx
- GHL Attribution: lib/ghl-attribution.ts + hooks/useGHLAttribution.ts
- GHL API: lib/ghl-api.ts
- GHL Form: components/GHLForm.tsx
- Page heroes: components/PageHero.tsx
- GHL Webhook: https://services.leadconnectorhq.com/hooks/ifVst8kd3WrSmJLqdJlQ/formCapture/website

## GHL Hidden Fields
Always include the full attribution field set in every form (see components/GHLForm.tsx).
Never remove UTM, click ID, or session tracking fields.

## Key Rules
- Use next/image for all images
- Use next/link for all internal links
- All forms POST to GHL webhook with full attribution payload
- Schedule page fetches from GHL Calendar API (lib/ghl-api.ts)
- Special offer page uses minimal layout (no full nav)
- Instructors page does NOT exist — never create or link to it
